  "id": "USN-9206-1",
  "summary": "guava-libraries vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that Guava did not correctly handle permissions for\ncertain temporary directories. An attacker could possibly use this issue\nto read or modify sensitive information. This issue only affected\nUbuntu 22.04 LTS. (CVE-2020-8908, CVE-2023-2976)\n\nKaya Emre Arikan discovered that Guava did not correctly handle\ndeserializing certain data. If a user or automated system were tricked\ninto opening a specially crafted file, an attacker could possibly use\nthis issue to cause a denial of service. (CVE-2026-102554)",
